    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d52">

                <pb facs="0115" n="31" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp02/pg31"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72114a/29</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Stovall</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berne</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-07-16T13:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 16, 1918, 1 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received July 17, 11 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3967. Department’s 1557, March 4, 4 p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d52-f1"/> I am
                    transmitting by mail a communication from German Foreign Office<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d52-f2"/> stating that German Government is disposed to enter into
                    same agreement with American Government regarding defense of prisoners of war
                    under accusation as exists between British and German Governments and French and
                    German Governments. The copy of <hi rendition="#italic">note verbale</hi> from
                    German Foreign Office to Netherlands Legation, Berlin, in charge of British
                    interests, giving conditions of agreement, is enclosed.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d52-f3"/>
                </p>
                <pb facs="0116" n="32" xml:id="pg32"/>
                <p>As regarding punishment for attempted escape, German Government is prepared to
                    reach agreement with United States Government and suggests that this question be
                    taken up in proposed prisoners-of-war conference at Berne.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d52-f4"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stovall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
